is when something clicks.

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:36.750
And you're like, you know--

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:39.200
When you really start to go crazy.

00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:40.333
That's what some people
may be thinking right now.

00:22:40.333 --> 00:22:44.100
It's like, if I've never
been alone that long,

00:22:44.100 --> 00:22:45.180
is that, are we talking about

00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:47.920
a breaking point or a break through point?

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:49.520
They might be one of the same.

00:22:50.860 --> 00:22:54.120
But this trip, for me, represents--

00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:56.826
But that's something,
your therapist tells you

00:22:56.826 --> 00:22:59.650
is that it doesn't need
to be a short trip.

00:22:59.650 --> 00:23:02.250
It needs to be as long as
you can make it so you can

00:23:03.840 --> 00:23:06.180
get past that turning point.

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:08.940
Well, and specifically,
and this is for me,

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:11.090
but it probably applies
to a lot of people.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.070
It takes a couple of days.

00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:14.903
I mean, I notice this

00:23:14.903 --> 00:23:17.610
when I travel on vacation
just with the family,

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:21.230
it takes a couple of days
for me to finally adjust

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:22.800
to the pace of a vacation.

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:24.380
I think about so many things.

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:29.310
I am constantly, have
a low level of anxiety

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:31.210
about like 28 different things

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:33.110
that are related to us professionally.

00:23:34.415 --> 00:23:36.493
I was thinking about
this the other day that,

00:23:37.490 --> 00:23:39.420
you guys know a lot of
the things that we do.

00:23:39.420 --> 00:23:42.310
You see a lot of the
things that we do publicly,

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:44.370
sort of the ongoing things that we do,

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:46.770
but we don't talk about what
it's like to run a company

00:23:46.770 --> 00:23:48.360
and to grow a company and to deal with

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:49.520
all the issues that come with that.

00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:51.800
We don't talk about all the other projects

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:52.840
that we're trying to get off the ground.

00:23:52.840 --> 00:23:54.460
We don't, there's a whole lot of things

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:55.300
that we don't talk about,

00:23:55.300 --> 00:23:57.180
just because we keep
some things to ourself.

00:23:57.180 --> 00:23:58.310
We talk about a lot.

00:23:58.310 --> 00:24:00.890
But sometimes it hits me,
even when I'm sitting down

00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:03.100
and trying to meditate, and
the point of the meditation

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:06.270
is to just focus on my breath

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:07.970
and not think about anything else.

00:24:09.090 --> 00:24:09.990
Monkey brain, right?

00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:13.540
I have monkey brain, just like
most everybody and I can't

00:24:13.540 --> 00:24:18.370
just stop thinking about a
million different things.

00:24:18.370 --> 00:24:22.330
So what I've been told by
people who try to unplug

00:24:22.330 --> 00:24:25.760
is that, listen, it takes
a few days just for,

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:29.646
to grab all the knobs and turn them off.

00:24:29.646 --> 00:24:32.630
You're just finding another
knob and turning it off.

00:24:32.630 --> 00:24:35.303
And for me, the whole
point of the trip is,

00:24:38.150 --> 00:24:43.150
I've been on this quest to try
to connect with myself more.

00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:46.660
And I don't say, I'm not saying
that in a self absorbed way,

00:24:46.660 --> 00:24:50.360
I'm saying that in a, I tend
to be very much in my head.

00:24:50.360 --> 00:24:52.340
Don't spend a lot of time in my heart.

00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:54.380
Don't spend a lot of
time understanding what,

00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:56.540
knowing what I'm feeling.

00:24:56.540 --> 00:24:58.170
Really getting into my feelings

00:24:58.170 --> 00:24:59.550
and understand what that means.

00:24:59.550 --> 00:25:01.810
Just knowing myself, right?

00:25:01.810 --> 00:25:04.850
And every step I've taken
towards that has been beneficial.

00:25:04.850 --> 00:25:05.683
Not only for me,

00:25:05.683 --> 00:25:07.760
but for all the people
in my life who I love.

00:25:08.750 --> 00:25:12.240
And I've been doing, one
sort of outward manifestation

00:25:12.240 --> 00:25:13.820
of what I'm trying to do internally

00:25:13.820 --> 00:25:15.530
has been me growing my
beard and my hair out.

00:25:15.530 --> 00:25:17.760
I talked about that on an
episode of Ear Biscuits.

00:25:17.760 --> 00:25:19.760
And I've been intending
to do this solo trip

00:25:19.760 --> 00:25:20.760
for a really long time,

00:25:20.760 --> 00:25:23.420
thinking that it was going to be 2020.

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:25.850
Of course COVID happened, and so things,

00:25:25.850 --> 00:25:28.200
a lot of people's plans
got turned upside down.

00:25:29.290 --> 00:25:31.063
But I finally got it on the books.

00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:34.990
You know, we said, let's
just carve the time out

00:25:34.990 --> 00:25:37.140
and then we'll start figuring
out what we're gonna do.

00:25:37.140 --> 00:25:38.590
So this was a couple of
months ago that we were like,

00:25:38.590 --> 00:25:40.535
okay, this is when the
time is going to be.

00:25:40.535 --> 00:25:45.535
It was before, before COVID hit, I think.

00:25:45.580 --> 00:25:47.050
It wasn't, it wasn't for me.

00:25:47.050 --> 00:25:51.393
I am going North from Los Angeles.

00:25:53.420 --> 00:25:56.730
One of the things that my
therapist has done many times,

00:25:56.730 --> 00:25:57.563
and is kind of into,

00:25:57.563 --> 00:25:59.560
is going throughout through
the Western United States

00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:00.520
and going to hot springs.

00:26:00.520 --> 00:26:01.890
And I'm a huge hot springs guy.

00:26:01.890 --> 00:26:04.350
I love hot springs. I love hot water.

00:26:04.350 --> 00:26:08.510
And I'm, I'm not, I don't
believe a lot of woo stuff.

00:26:08.510 --> 00:26:10.380
So I'm not, I don't necessarily think

00:26:10.380 --> 00:26:11.990
that there's some like spiritual thing

00:26:11.990 --> 00:26:13.610
that's gonna happen to
me at these hot springs.

00:26:13.610 --> 00:26:15.990
Maybe I'm open to it, but
that's not why I'm going.

00:26:15.990 --> 00:26:18.500
I just love hot springs.
And I love the idea.

00:26:18.500 --> 00:26:21.360
He sent me these pictures
of places he's gone,

00:26:21.360 --> 00:26:24.740
where he drives his
four wheel drive vehicle

00:26:24.740 --> 00:26:26.950
through these mountains and
comes to this hot spring.

00:26:26.950 --> 00:26:29.610
And then he's got this
hot spring to himself.

00:26:29.610 --> 00:26:31.904
And there's nobody there.
I mean, it is really cool.

00:26:31.904 --> 00:26:32.787
It's mesmerizing to think about it.

00:26:32.787 --> 00:26:37.200
'Cause you look on a map
and you can see, I mean,

00:26:37.200 --> 00:26:38.940
when we've gone off-roading,

00:26:38.940 --> 00:26:42.140
our first experience with
hot springs was when we went

00:26:42.140 --> 00:26:44.580
on that trip to Death Valley.

00:26:44.580 --> 00:26:46.670
And then you get to this one little oasis

00:26:46.670 --> 00:26:48.810
in the middle of this
valley that has nothing.

00:26:48.810 --> 00:26:51.500
But way down there in
the bottom of the valley

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:53.580
You see there's some palm trees.

00:26:53.580 --> 00:26:56.850
I mean, just what you
would think of an oasis.

00:26:56.850 --> 00:26:59.560
And there was a hot spring there

00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:01.800
and there was some naked people.

00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:04.760
We talked about that on a GMM
episode when we came back.

00:27:04.760 --> 00:27:07.900
And those are more, that's like on a road

00:27:07.900 --> 00:27:10.240
that most cars can get
to, there might be an RV.

00:27:10.240 --> 00:27:11.680
Some of the ones that he's shown me,

00:27:11.680 --> 00:27:14.030
that I may or may not be able to get to,

00:27:14.030 --> 00:27:15.190
are more isolated than that.

00:27:15.190 --> 00:27:18.260
Yeah. You'll just see on the
map, it'd say hot springs,

00:27:18.260 --> 00:27:19.960
but it looks like it's
in the middle of nowhere.

00:27:19.960 --> 00:27:22.673
And some of them don't even,
aren't even on the map.

00:27:23.730 --> 00:27:25.553
So, okay. So anyway.

00:27:26.880 --> 00:27:27.760
This is where I,

00:27:27.760 --> 00:27:29.300
and I don't want to get
too in the weeds on this,

00:27:29.300 --> 00:27:34.300
but the thing that is very,
sort of the key struggle

00:27:34.520 --> 00:27:36.100
that I'm dealing with at this point,

00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:37.780
two days out from departure,

00:27:37.780 --> 00:27:39.970
is what I've been dealing
with for the past two months.

00:27:39.970 --> 00:27:43.680
Which is the balance of being prepared

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:49.820
versus having unrealistic or
even specific expectations.

00:27:49.820 --> 00:27:52.060
Because for me, the whole exercise,

00:27:52.060 --> 00:27:54.320
the whole point of the trip,

00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:57.980
is to not want to accomplish anything.

00:27:57.980 --> 00:27:59.190
My life

00:28:00.408 --> 00:28:03.590
and my brain is sort
of completely centered

00:28:03.590 --> 00:28:06.320
around accomplishing things, right?

00:28:06.320 --> 00:28:08.590
And I can't vacation without thinking

00:28:08.590 --> 00:28:11.090
that I need to learn how to do,
I need to learn how to surf.

00:28:11.090 --> 00:28:13.640
I need to, I have these
things that I get in my mind

00:28:13.640 --> 00:28:15.140
that I feel like I have to accomplish

00:28:15.140 --> 00:28:16.800
in order to make it worth it.

00:28:16.800 --> 00:28:19.230
And when you go on a solo
trip, there is this like,

00:28:19.230 --> 00:28:21.750
well, I've got to come
back with some wisdom.

00:28:21.750 --> 00:28:23.873
I've gotta come back with something.

00:28:25.210 --> 00:28:29.080
But also I, what if I
can't find these places?

00:28:29.080 --> 00:28:31.130
Or what if I get there
and there's people there?

00:28:31.130 --> 00:28:34.930
What if I get there, and
the big, huge question mark

00:28:34.930 --> 00:28:36.810
that has suddenly sprung up in these plans

00:28:36.810 --> 00:28:40.410
is the freaking wildfires
that are consuming our state.

00:28:40.410 --> 00:28:41.850
And I'm not driving.

00:28:41.850 --> 00:28:44.670
I am driving directly towards one of them,

00:28:44.670 --> 00:28:47.850
but it's one that's not as
big as some of the other ones.

00:28:47.850 --> 00:28:49.660
But if you look at satellite imagery

00:28:49.660 --> 00:28:51.900
of the state of California,
there's smoke everywhere.

00:28:51.900 --> 00:28:53.730
I mean, wherever I go,

00:28:53.730 --> 00:28:54.860
I'm going to be

00:28:56.480 --> 00:28:58.560
covered in smoke to some degree.

00:28:58.560 --> 00:29:00.970
And not only that, but just last night,

00:29:00.970 --> 00:29:02.883
because of this latest fire,

00:29:03.768 --> 00:29:05.420
it was a bunch of fires
that just happened.

00:29:05.420 --> 00:29:07.070
Having just started recording those.

00:29:07.070 --> 00:29:09.340
I mean, there's been
multiple fires, but there's

00:29:09.340 --> 00:29:11.630
a couple more that just
started over the weekend.

00:29:11.630 --> 00:29:13.780
And now the Santa Ana winds are coming in.

00:29:13.780 --> 00:29:17.600
They've closed all the national forest.

00:29:17.600 --> 00:29:20.543
So like Sequoia's closed,

00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:23.460
Inyo is closed.

00:29:23.460 --> 00:29:25.650
And both Sequoia and
Inyo, especially Inyo,

00:29:25.650 --> 00:29:27.880
are ones that I would
have been camping in.

00:29:27.880 --> 00:29:28.810
That's right, yeah.

00:29:28.810 --> 00:29:32.520
And so I don't know what that
means for all the BLM land.

00:29:32.520 --> 00:29:34.350
'Cause you've got the
Bureau of Land Management,

00:29:34.350 --> 00:29:37.330
which is like, usually crappier land,

00:29:37.330 --> 00:29:39.050
that wasn't good enough to be designated

00:29:39.050 --> 00:29:41.570
as a national park or a forest,

00:29:41.570 --> 00:29:43.250
but you can do disperse camping.

00:29:43.250 --> 00:29:47.430
And I've got this rooftop
tent on the FJ cruiser.

00:29:47.430 --> 00:29:48.297
That, basically,

00:29:48.297 --> 00:29:50.440
if I could find a place
to park, I can camp.

00:29:50.440 --> 00:29:54.060
But there are no fires
allowed, and not just no fires,

00:29:54.060 --> 00:29:57.150
no stoves, no gas stoves.

00:29:57.150 --> 00:29:59.133
So you can't even get hot water.

00:30:00.568 --> 00:30:05.360
As of last night, you
cannot have a gas stove fire

00:30:05.360 --> 00:30:09.370
anywhere in a national
forest in California.

00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:11.400
But that, what does that mean about BLM?

00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:14.820
I've got my little bullet water boiler

00:30:14.820 --> 00:30:19.040
that I'm just, to make
like quick meals and stuff.

00:30:19.040 --> 00:30:23.390
I won't do that in a forest,
in a national forest.

00:30:23.390 --> 00:30:26.700
But I'm going to do it on
BLM land 'cause I got to eat.

00:30:26.700 --> 00:30:28.100
But I mean, there's no fire risk in that.

00:30:28.100 --> 00:30:30.390
What you don't need to
do is you don't need

00:30:30.390 --> 00:30:32.810
to fire off one of those
gender reveal rockets.

00:30:32.810 --> 00:30:34.270
Basically, that's where this is all about.

00:30:34.270 --> 00:30:35.550
I'm going to go into the desert

00:30:35.550 --> 00:30:38.060
and do a gender reveal of myself.

00:30:38.060 --> 00:30:40.368
That's why, I mean, that's what it said,

00:30:40.368 --> 00:30:42.270
that the fire South of us started

00:30:42.270 --> 00:30:43.703
by a freaking gender reveal party.

00:30:43.703 --> 00:30:44.536
I know.

00:30:44.536 --> 00:30:45.369
Well, why, what are they doing

00:30:45.369 --> 00:30:47.100
having a gender reveal party?

00:30:47.100 --> 00:30:50.220
And it was over a hundred
degrees and they're outside

00:30:50.220 --> 00:30:54.780
firing off a pink or blue
smoke that caught fire.

00:30:54.780 --> 00:30:55.970
They tried to put it out.

00:30:55.970 --> 00:30:57.600
It goes over the hill

00:30:57.600 --> 00:31:00.340
and then they evacuating
thousands of people.

00:31:00.340 --> 00:31:02.620
And did you hear what they're saying?

00:31:02.620 --> 00:31:04.410
They're going to--
Nightmare.

00:31:04.410 --> 00:31:09.410
They're going to make
that family be responsible

00:31:09.450 --> 00:31:11.323
to pay for the damage of the fire.

00:31:12.540 --> 00:31:14.850
What do you mean? Are they billionaires?

00:31:14.850 --> 00:31:16.970
Cause otherwise, no.

00:31:16.970 --> 00:31:19.100
I mean, they should obviously
be held accountable,

00:31:19.100 --> 00:31:22.100
but I saw an article
like family has to pay.

00:31:22.100 --> 00:31:23.480
I was like, pay? Out of what?

00:31:23.480 --> 00:31:24.890
They're sorry. That's all you can,

00:31:24.890 --> 00:31:28.833
I mean, they learnt, they've
been made an example of.

00:31:28.833 --> 00:31:31.281
So that's complicating
things because fires are--

00:31:31.281 --> 00:31:32.980
Fires are so sad.

00:31:32.980 --> 00:31:35.610
I don't have a, I have,

00:31:35.610 --> 00:31:39.020
I've got all these apps and
all these maps downloaded.

00:31:39.020 --> 00:31:40.990
And I've got like, my family laughs at me

00:31:40.990 --> 00:31:43.770
because every single weekend I'm out there

00:31:43.770 --> 00:31:45.040
putting stuff into the truck

00:31:45.040 --> 00:31:48.310
and I've got these drawers
in the back of the FJ now

00:31:48.310 --> 00:31:49.330
with all my stuff in it.

00:31:49.330 --> 00:31:52.020
I am so prepared.

00:31:52.020 --> 00:31:53.970
And I'm really excited
about the rooftop tent.

00:31:53.970 --> 00:31:55.170
Oh yeah, that's nice.

00:31:55.170 --> 00:31:56.543
But my route--

00:31:56.543 --> 00:31:57.660
I plan on using that.

00:31:57.660 --> 00:32:00.633
My route takes me up into,

00:32:02.040 --> 00:32:03.910
basically heading up towards Mammoth

00:32:03.910 --> 00:32:07.350
and that whole valley
all the way up on the 395

00:32:07.350 --> 00:32:09.450
has got, there's hot springs and stuff.

00:32:09.450 --> 00:32:14.450
And then my options after
that, depending on how I feel,

00:32:14.760 --> 00:32:18.620
I could go all the way
up to Northern Nevada.

00:32:18.620 --> 00:32:22.070
I could go all the way
to Idaho if it hits me.

00:32:22.070 --> 00:32:24.066
But I think I'm going to get
too far away at that point.

00:32:24.066 --> 00:32:25.077
And it would be too tough to come back.

00:32:25.077 --> 00:32:27.750
But there's wildfires
all along this route.

00:32:27.750 --> 00:32:31.320
And so I just don't
know, every single night

00:32:31.320 --> 00:32:33.750
I'm going to have an
intention on the general area

00:32:33.750 --> 00:32:36.403
in which I would like to
sleep and kind of bed down.

00:32:37.400 --> 00:32:40.230
But it's so up in the air, there's no,

00:32:40.230 --> 00:32:41.840
I'm not doing any formal campgrounds.

00:32:41.840 --> 00:32:46.680
I have a portable toilet
with a privacy pop-up thing.

00:32:46.680 --> 00:32:48.340
I have a solar shower.

00:32:48.340 --> 00:32:50.950
I am going to be
completely self sufficient.

00:32:50.950 --> 00:32:53.200
I don't have to stop
anywhere except for gas.

00:32:55.300 --> 00:32:57.700
Let me share my plans a little bit.

00:32:57.700 --> 00:33:00.280
And, cause I, and then
I want to come back to

00:33:02.020 --> 00:33:05.180
what is going to be your practice,

00:33:05.180 --> 00:33:07.020
'cause I'm, I'm interested in that.

00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:10.210
But just to kind of skip over to my thing.

00:33:10.210 --> 00:33:11.810
Yeah, once you carved out those dates,

00:33:11.810 --> 00:33:14.097
it's so much easier to say,

00:33:14.097 --> 00:33:17.137
"Oh, I'm going to do the same dates.

00:33:17.137 --> 00:33:19.490
"I'm going to plan my own trip."

00:33:19.490 --> 00:33:24.490
And I really like the idea
of doing another solo trip.

00:33:24.970 --> 00:33:28.860
And I definitely have
this feeling that I could

00:33:28.860 --> 00:33:31.660
really benefit from that and
I definitely want to do it.

00:33:32.980 --> 00:33:37.050
But I've had this thing that,
I've told you about the vans.

00:33:37.050 --> 00:33:40.060
I started this hashtag vanlife stuff.

00:33:40.060 --> 00:33:41.480
I've started following all these people

00:33:41.480 --> 00:33:44.520
who live out of these
Mercedes Sprinter vans

00:33:44.520 --> 00:33:47.090
that have been modded out
with a bed and a kitchen.

00:33:47.090 --> 00:33:49.300
And some of them have a bathroom inside

00:33:49.300 --> 00:33:51.100
and they can have four wheel drive.

00:33:51.100 --> 00:33:53.610
Oh, it just looks so good on Instagram.

00:33:53.610 --> 00:33:56.320
Oh, just look at those
pictures of that person.

00:33:56.320 --> 00:33:58.850
Just a van in the middle of nowhere.

00:33:58.850 --> 00:34:03.850
And I'm like, I can see this in my future.

00:34:04.300 --> 00:34:05.545
And I start talking to you about--

00:34:05.545 --> 00:34:06.610
You can see it in you're future.

00:34:06.610 --> 00:34:07.443
I'm gonna get one of these vans.

00:34:07.443 --> 00:34:09.160
Can you see it in Christy's future?

00:34:09.160 --> 00:34:11.210
Because it's in her future an this point.

00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:15.270
Yes, I'm really
romanticizing this idea of,

00:34:15.270 --> 00:34:17.210
not selling my house and living in a van,

00:34:17.210 --> 00:34:19.900
but having this van,

00:34:19.900 --> 00:34:23.480
it's basically the cool
hipster version of an RV.

00:34:23.480 --> 00:34:26.840
We had our RV trip to Grand
Canyon a few years back

00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:29.510
and Lando was excited to do it again

00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:33.788
and Christy had a good
time but the older kids,

00:34:33.788 --> 00:34:36.980
it just didn't resonate
that much with them.

00:34:36.980 --> 00:34:40.290
And I'm like, well, I
can see in retirement,

00:34:40.290 --> 00:34:42.130
me and Christy are gonna--

00:34:42.130 --> 00:34:42.963
Be that couple.

00:34:42.963 --> 00:34:46.060
It's like, once Lando is out of the house.

00:34:46.060 --> 00:34:47.260
So like, you know--

00:34:47.260 --> 00:34:48.950
Yeah, when he's 14, you're
going to send them off early.

00:34:48.950 --> 00:34:51.450
Well let's just say eight years from now.

00:34:51.450 --> 00:34:54.738
It's like, I could see that we
could do something like that.

00:34:54.738 --> 00:34:58.937
Me and Christy could just
have these van excursions.

00:34:58.937 --> 00:35:01.290
And she can see this as well?

00:35:01.290 --> 00:35:03.990
I'm starting, I started to
show her pictures on Instagram.

00:35:03.990 --> 00:35:07.372
I was like, isn't that cool?
Look at where they are.

00:35:07.372 --> 00:35:08.237
How does she respond to that?

00:35:08.237 --> 00:35:11.250
There's this specific
one that floats around.

00:35:11.250 --> 00:35:15.290
And it's a point of view shot of someone

00:35:15.290 --> 00:35:18.510
