in their Sprinter van,

00:35:18.510 --> 00:35:23.510
going over to the burner and
taking the hot coffee in a mug,

00:35:23.620 --> 00:35:26.680
opening the door to the
Sprinter van and then--

00:35:26.680 --> 00:35:27.513
I've seen this.

00:35:27.513 --> 00:35:30.230
Jump, then walking out
of the Sprinter van,

00:35:30.230 --> 00:35:32.740
walking onto this little
dock and then jumping

00:35:32.740 --> 00:35:36.020
into this beautiful mountain
lake, with the coffee.

00:35:36.020 --> 00:35:37.790
Are you going to make those
kinds of videos on your trip?

00:35:37.790 --> 00:35:39.760
And I'm like, I'm showing this to her.

00:35:39.760 --> 00:35:43.110
And I'm like, we're going to
make these types of videos

00:35:43.110 --> 00:35:44.520
in our retirement years.

00:35:44.520 --> 00:35:47.320
And then I'm like, you know
what? Screw retirement.

00:35:47.320 --> 00:35:50.730
I want to know now if this is even viable.

00:35:50.730 --> 00:35:55.160
So I bought one. No. You can
rent these Sprinter vans.

00:35:55.160 --> 00:35:58.410
This is like, there's a
site called outdoorsy,

00:35:58.410 --> 00:36:00.429
which is like the Airbnb for RVs.

00:36:00.429 --> 00:36:02.973
Does the having a bathroom?

00:36:04.060 --> 00:36:06.110
The first one I was going to
rent didn't have a bathroom.

00:36:06.110 --> 00:36:08.640
But then I was like, you know what?

00:36:08.640 --> 00:36:12.060
This is so much about, so much hinges

00:36:12.060 --> 00:36:15.040
on us having a good
experience, me and Christy.

00:36:15.040 --> 00:36:16.120
And again, it's just the two of us.

00:36:16.120 --> 00:36:17.970
We're not taking the kids.

00:36:17.970 --> 00:36:22.970
It's like, if she hates this,
there's, I see no way forward.

00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:25.503
Is this a bathroom you can take a shit in?

00:36:26.420 --> 00:36:28.180
So I'm like, I'm renting
one with the bathroom.

00:36:28.180 --> 00:36:31.330
So it's a toilet that,
yeah, you can crap in there.

00:36:31.330 --> 00:36:33.800
