00:37:01.630 --> 00:37:02.970
No, well, I don't know.

00:37:02.970 --> 00:37:04.080
Maybe the technology's gotten better.

00:37:04.080 --> 00:37:05.033
You have to test it out.

00:37:05.033 --> 00:37:06.120
I can sus it out for you.

00:37:06.120 --> 00:37:09.410
There's a seal. There's definitely--

00:37:09.410 --> 00:37:10.676
There's a seal down there that eats it.

00:37:15.028 --> 00:37:16.470
That's why it costs so much, '

00:37:16.470 --> 00:37:19.080
cause you have to have an
environment for a seal.

00:37:19.080 --> 00:37:21.286
That poor seal, man.

00:37:21.286 --> 00:37:23.200
That's what you should feel bad about,

00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:24.280
that you got to seal this that's eating

00:37:24.280 --> 00:37:28.023
you and your wife's crap the whole trip.

00:37:29.184 --> 00:37:31.130
C thought Sea World was bad.

00:37:31.130 --> 00:37:34.013
And it's.

00:37:35.590 --> 00:37:37.150
When we did the RV it was like,

00:37:37.150 --> 00:37:40.480
there was no crapping in the
RV toilet, that was our rule.

00:37:40.480 --> 00:37:41.313
Just like when we were on tour.

00:37:41.313 --> 00:37:44.140
And that was based on
our experience in 2008,

00:37:44.140 --> 00:37:45.660
being on an RV and somebody saying,

00:37:45.660 --> 00:37:47.390
don't nobody crap in this thing.

00:37:47.390 --> 00:37:49.670
No, but we gonna crap in this thing,

00:37:49.670 --> 00:37:50.740
and we're going to figure it out.

00:37:50.740 --> 00:37:52.873
We're going to see,
that's part of the test.

00:37:53.740 --> 00:37:55.200
Otherwise these other Sprinter vans

00:37:55.200 --> 00:37:58.970
that don't want to dedicate
the internal space to a shower,

00:37:58.970 --> 00:38:01.950
they'll have a shower hanging off the back

00:38:01.950 --> 00:38:04.060
and then they have a portable
toilet, like what you have,

00:38:04.060 --> 00:38:06.030
and you just you'll just do
it in the middle of the van

00:38:06.030 --> 00:38:07.670
or you'll do it with a curtain around you.

00:38:07.670 --> 00:38:08.980
What you're talking about mine.

00:38:08.980 --> 00:38:13.980
Yeah, mine is a, it is a, it
folds up to like a briefcase,

00:38:14.450 --> 00:38:17.280
but then the legs come out,
and then you sit on it,

00:38:17.280 --> 00:38:19.810
and there's a bag that basically,

00:38:19.810 --> 00:38:21.473
and I've got like 12 bags or something.

00:38:21.473 --> 00:38:22.920
Like a Diaper Genie?

00:38:22.920 --> 00:38:24.940
It's basically like a diaper kind of bag.

00:38:24.940 --> 00:38:27.150
And so, and I was reading the reviews

00:38:27.150 --> 00:38:29.207
and this one mom was like,

00:38:29.207 --> 00:38:33.550
"Our family of five used one
bag for the three day trip."

00:38:33.550 --> 00:38:34.460
And I'm like, what?

00:38:34.460 --> 00:38:37.090
But see, I think, what it
is is you take that bag

00:38:37.090 --> 00:38:40.080
and you seal it up and then you put it.

00:38:40.080 --> 00:38:42.249
So I've got the trasharoo which is my out,

00:38:42.249 --> 00:38:44.780
it's the trash on the
outside of the truck,

00:38:44.780 --> 00:38:46.420
that's on the back spare.

00:38:46.420 --> 00:38:47.710
And then I think you just take that bag

00:38:47.710 --> 00:38:49.470
and you put it out there, so it's outside.

00:38:49.470 --> 00:38:50.530
And so it's not in your car.

00:38:50.530 --> 00:38:51.760
You can't do that in bear country,

00:38:51.760 --> 00:38:53.810
but I don't think you're
going to bear country.

00:38:53.810 --> 00:38:54.770
You're going to--

00:38:54.770 --> 00:38:56.367
Yeah, well I would be going,

00:38:56.367 --> 00:38:59.150
and I do have bear spray, by the way,

00:38:59.150 --> 00:39:01.500
I've got two cans of bear spray.

00:39:01.500 --> 00:39:03.860
If I go to the West of 395, which is where

00:39:03.860 --> 00:39:06.310
you're getting up closer to
the Sequoia and everything,

00:39:06.310 --> 00:39:08.815
that's bear country, If I
were to go hiking or whatever.

00:39:08.815 --> 00:39:09.740
But you're not going there anymore.

00:39:09.740 --> 00:39:11.360
But the problem is, is that's
where all the fires are.

00:39:11.360 --> 00:39:12.950
So I'm probably going
to go on the East side.

00:39:12.950 --> 00:39:14.287
There might be bears out there.

00:39:14.287 --> 00:39:17.320
You're saying the bears,
you're not talking,

00:39:17.320 --> 00:39:19.450
you're talking about just the
trash being on the outside?

00:39:19.450 --> 00:39:20.923
Yeah, yeah.
Yeah, yeah.

00:39:21.940 --> 00:39:23.810
If I'm in a place that I
think that there's bears

00:39:23.810 --> 00:39:25.670
then I'll put everything inside.

00:39:25.670 --> 00:39:27.880
So you can boondock,

00:39:27.880 --> 00:39:29.770
which is basically you can camp in your,

00:39:29.770 --> 00:39:34.770
you can car camp anywhere
that is X amount of feet

00:39:35.260 --> 00:39:40.260
off of a road on either
national forest or BLM land.

00:39:40.990 --> 00:39:44.930
And you can't start fires everywhere,

00:39:44.930 --> 00:39:46.720
or really anywhere right now.

00:39:46.720 --> 00:39:48.630
But you have this,
there's a sense of freedom

00:39:48.630 --> 00:39:51.260
that you don't have to reserve a campsite.

00:39:51.260 --> 00:39:54.040
I mean, with COVID you can't
really reserve campsites

00:39:54.040 --> 00:39:58.260
anywhere that's that the
best destinations anyway,

00:39:58.260 --> 00:39:59.470
they were already reserved

00:39:59.470 --> 00:40:03.270
and the capacity was severely taken down.

00:40:03.270 --> 00:40:07.600
But my plan was, we were
going to go up the coast

00:40:07.600 --> 00:40:10.453
to Big Sur and we were going to,

00:40:11.870 --> 00:40:13.280
we're going to camp there one night

00:40:13.280 --> 00:40:15.210
and then we're going to
keep going up to Monterey.

00:40:15.210 --> 00:40:17.890
And then we're going to
go across to Yosemite.

00:40:17.890 --> 00:40:21.230
I mean, when I made these plans,
the state was not burning.

00:40:21.230 --> 00:40:25.730
But then all of a sudden
Big Sur caught on fire.

00:40:25.730 --> 00:40:26.563
Yeah, it's all burning.

00:40:26.563 --> 00:40:27.960
So I was like, well that's
going off of the list.

00:40:27.960 --> 00:40:29.570
I'm just going to go to Yosemite

00:40:30.450 --> 00:40:32.730
and we can stay outside of the park.

00:40:32.730 --> 00:40:34.860
There's places you can stay,

00:40:34.860 --> 00:40:37.490
spots you can stay at, I should say.

00:40:37.490 --> 00:40:41.262
But now the air quality there is so bad.

00:40:41.262 --> 00:40:45.350
The fires, at least right
now, aren't in Yosemite,

00:40:45.350 --> 00:40:47.310
but there's so much smoke coming in

00:40:47.310 --> 00:40:49.970
that it is not going to
be a good experience.

00:40:49.970 --> 00:40:51.400
There's still a chance we may go,

00:40:51.400 --> 00:40:53.484
but I'm pretty much have decided

00:40:53.484 --> 00:40:55.080
that we're not going to Yosemite.

00:40:55.080 --> 00:40:58.600
So now I'm like, I was
literally just looking at

00:40:58.600 --> 00:41:01.270
the fire map of the
Western United States and

00:41:01.270 --> 00:41:04.940
trying to figure out where we
could go that wasn't on fire.

00:41:04.940 --> 00:41:08.023
And I was like, I think
Utah is hard to burn.

00:41:10.715 --> 00:41:13.840
'Cause if you look at, just
based on the fire maps,

00:41:14.800 --> 00:41:16.550
now I think I'm going to Utah.

00:41:16.550 --> 00:41:18.880
Now Zion is very restricted.

00:41:18.880 --> 00:41:20.460
Yeah, you got to get a
shuttle to go in there.

00:41:20.460 --> 00:41:22.492
So I don't think we're
going to Zion National Park.

00:41:22.492 --> 00:41:26.160
But, my understanding,
because I may end up in Utah.

00:41:26.160 --> 00:41:31.160
So my route, one of my routes
takes me all the way to Utah

00:41:32.650 --> 00:41:37.340
and then down through Zion,
and I'm just, I would still

00:41:37.340 --> 00:41:40.920
just be on BLM, National
Forest land and stuff,

00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:42.860
not going into the actual national parks.

00:41:42.860 --> 00:41:44.240
If you get too far into Utah,

00:41:44.240 --> 00:41:45.620
there's just not a lot of burn.

00:41:45.620 --> 00:41:47.570
I mean, I'm speaking out of turn here,

00:41:47.570 --> 00:41:48.963
but that's just the impression I get.

00:41:48.963 --> 00:41:52.530
It's a bunch of rock
formation, there's no forests.

00:41:52.530 --> 00:41:55.910
That's why all the fires
are West of the 395,

00:41:55.910 --> 00:41:59.210
because even on the Eastern side of the,

00:41:59.210 --> 00:42:01.200
so I guess that's the Eastern Sierras.

00:42:01.200 --> 00:42:02.790
You just look at a satellite map.

00:42:02.790 --> 00:42:06.360
It's like, it's, there's just
not a lot of vegetation there.

00:42:06.360 --> 00:42:09.400
But I'm trying to find a
place that's not wicked hot.

00:42:09.400 --> 00:42:12.070
It's not going to be
that hot at elevation.

00:42:12.070 --> 00:42:14.100
I think we're going to Bryce Canyon,

00:42:14.100 --> 00:42:15.300
or we're going around that area.

00:42:15.300 --> 00:42:18.060
But again, we're just gonna,
we can find places to,

00:42:18.060 --> 00:42:19.480
we're doing the same thing you're doing.

00:42:19.480 --> 00:42:22.530
I'm just doing it in a really nice van.

00:42:22.530 --> 00:42:25.920
So that I'm glamping and
you're just roughing it.

00:42:25.920 --> 00:42:28.790
I mean, mine's gonna be,
it's not really roughing it.

00:42:28.790 --> 00:42:32.010
I mean, this, it's not,

00:42:32.010 --> 00:42:36.240
it's not glamping, but it's
easier than regular camp.

00:42:36.240 --> 00:42:39.630
And the, I mean, the whole idea for me

00:42:40.620 --> 00:42:42.460
is the, is to be like,

00:42:42.460 --> 00:42:45.210
I don't know exactly where
I'm gonna park tonight

00:42:45.210 --> 00:42:47.970
and then roll this tent out.

00:42:47.970 --> 00:42:51.240
I want to be alone, right?

00:42:51.240 --> 00:42:53.810
And so my philosophy, going into this,

00:42:53.810 --> 00:42:58.250
is I'm driving North,
kinda gonna feel it out.

00:42:58.250 --> 00:43:01.750
And I'm doing as much as I can

00:43:01.750 --> 00:43:04.945
to literally like follow my instincts,

00:43:04.945 --> 00:43:06.745
follow my heart, wherever might go.

00:43:06.745 --> 00:43:07.873
It's an embodiment practice, right?

00:43:07.873 --> 00:43:10.680
It's like, I'm physically going somewhere.

00:43:10.680 --> 00:43:12.270
I don't have specific plans

00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:13.610
and I'm going to take it as it comes.

00:43:13.610 --> 00:43:16.380
And I'm gonna try to have an attitude,

00:43:16.380 --> 00:43:18.540
correct me if I'm wrong, of embracing

00:43:19.430 --> 00:43:21.076
whatever situation presents itself.

00:43:21.076 --> 00:43:22.757
No expectations.

00:43:22.757 --> 00:43:25.160
And that is a very difficult
thing for me to do,

00:43:25.160 --> 00:43:28.420
because I'm thinking about
like, I've been looking at this,

00:43:28.420 --> 00:43:30.390
looking at these maps and like thinking,

00:43:30.390 --> 00:43:31.740
oh, I could go to this one.

00:43:32.840 --> 00:43:34.440
Or am I going to be in
the mood to drive that far

00:43:34.440 --> 00:43:35.370
if I want to go to this one?

00:43:35.370 --> 00:43:38.560
What if I get there and it's
closed because of the fires?

00:43:38.560 --> 00:43:40.590
Or it's closed for some other reason?

00:43:40.590 --> 00:43:41.920
Or there's just a bunch of people there,

00:43:41.920 --> 00:43:45.010
and I can't like, or in
many of these places,

00:43:45.010 --> 00:43:46.130
there's a bunch of naked people there.

00:43:46.130 --> 00:43:48.860
I don't mind that, but what
if I wanted to get naked?

00:43:48.860 --> 00:43:49.693
Am I gonna get naked

00:43:49.693 --> 00:43:51.960
with a bunch of people that I don't know?

00:43:51.960 --> 00:43:53.530
Anything's on the table.

00:43:53.530 --> 00:43:56.880
So the whole, the exercise is to let go.

00:43:56.880 --> 00:43:59.420
Are you, if you show up
at a place, a spring,

00:43:59.420 --> 00:44:02.510
and there's naked people there,
what are you going to do?

00:44:02.510 --> 00:44:07.510
I'm just gonna get in with
my bathing suit on, probably.

00:44:08.480 --> 00:44:11.290
If they're naked?
Yeah. I don't, I mean--

00:44:11.290 --> 00:44:12.123
Just be naked.

00:44:12.123 --> 00:44:12.956
I haven't thought about it. You know what?

00:44:12.956 --> 00:44:14.178
I'm going to wait

00:44:14.178 --> 00:44:16.090
and I'm going to follow
my heart in the moment.

00:44:16.090 --> 00:44:18.170
If my heart says, let it all hang out.

00:44:18.170 --> 00:44:20.800
It is going to be hard.
It would be hard for me,

00:44:20.800 --> 00:44:23.860
I'll put it this way,
to not be thinking about

00:44:24.770 --> 00:44:27.200
the report that I would
come back and give to you.

00:44:27.200 --> 00:44:30.357
I mean the last solo trip, it,

00:44:30.357 --> 00:44:33.210
there was meaningful things that happened.

00:44:33.210 --> 00:44:36.420
But I do remember
constantly thinking about

00:44:36.420 --> 00:44:37.943
how it was going to,

00:44:39.536 --> 00:44:42.340
what kind of stories I was
going to be able to tell

00:44:42.340 --> 00:44:45.090
that would make it more valuable,

00:44:45.090 --> 00:44:47.960
but not in, that's not
the value you seek here.

00:44:47.960 --> 00:44:50.450
But I talked, so I
talked about this aspect.

00:44:50.450 --> 00:44:53.400
I actually, I hesitated
even talking about this trip

00:44:53.400 --> 00:44:55.500
for this very reason, right?

00:44:55.500 --> 00:44:58.760
And I talked about this whole
process with my therapist.

00:44:58.760 --> 00:45:00.720
'Cause I said, I have a tendency

00:45:01.800 --> 00:45:04.050
for a couple of things to happen.

00:45:04.050 --> 00:45:06.460
Number one, I can be so focused on

00:45:07.620 --> 00:45:10.270
not accomplishing something that,

00:45:10.270 --> 00:45:14.103
that becomes something
I'm trying to accomplish.

00:45:15.090 --> 00:45:17.500
I'm so focused on letting go that

00:45:17.500 --> 00:45:18.880
if I feel like I can't let go,

00:45:18.880 --> 00:45:21.730
then I feel like I haven't
met the expectation

00:45:21.730 --> 00:45:23.920
of letting go of expectations.

00:45:23.920 --> 00:45:26.600
So you really get inside
your own head, right?

00:45:26.600 --> 00:45:28.080
But the other thing is,

00:45:28.080 --> 00:45:32.017
is I think that I have to
have something to bring back.

00:45:32.017 --> 00:45:35.550
And that can be, this is what happened

00:45:35.550 --> 00:45:38.730
in my mind and my heart
while I was on this trip.

00:45:38.730 --> 00:45:41.070
This is the epiphany that I had.

00:45:41.070 --> 00:45:43.870
This is the realization that I had

00:45:43.870 --> 00:45:46.180
at the third day, in the
middle of a meditation,

00:45:46.180 --> 00:45:48.673
while I was tracking the sun, you know?

00:45:49.570 --> 00:45:52.260
Or some funny has gotta happen.

00:45:52.260 --> 00:45:53.550
So I've got the story

00:45:53.550 --> 00:45:55.420
of whether or not I got
naked at the spring,

00:45:55.420 --> 00:45:57.950
so I can come back on
Ear Biscuits and tell it.

00:45:57.950 --> 00:46:01.400
And so my mission,

00:46:01.400 --> 00:46:03.050
and again, there's really no way

00:46:03.050 --> 00:46:05.390
to let go of this seeming like a mission

00:46:05.390 --> 00:46:08.900
is to not have a mission
and to literally be like,

00:46:08.900 --> 00:46:11.140
I don't, I'm not trying to
get myself into situation.

00:46:11.140 --> 00:46:12.270
I'm not trying to take,

00:46:12.270 --> 00:46:16.790
a lot of times we'll do
something or take a risk.

00:46:16.790 --> 00:46:21.063
Like the time that I went to
that yoga class on my, solo,

00:46:22.940 --> 00:46:25.090
we've taken a couple of solo.

00:46:25.090 --> 00:46:27.230
I went to Joshua Tree one time.

00:46:27.230 --> 00:46:30.660
But then another solo trip
is when I went to the beach

00:46:30.660 --> 00:46:32.220
and I took in that yoga class.

00:46:32.220 --> 00:46:33.240
And I was the only guy in there.

00:46:33.240 --> 00:46:34.713
And it was a hilarious story.

00:46:36.290 --> 00:46:37.960
There's a part of me that
went to that yoga class,

00:46:37.960 --> 00:46:39.320
knowing that something funny might happen

00:46:39.320 --> 00:46:40.888
that I could talk about on Ear Biscuits.

00:46:40.888 --> 00:46:43.460
And I like living life
like that in certain ways,

00:46:43.460 --> 00:46:45.520
in some ways, because I feel like

00:46:45.520 --> 00:46:48.150
it leads me into better experiences.

00:46:48.150 --> 00:46:51.940
But for this trip, I can't even promise

00:46:51.940 --> 00:46:54.400
that I'm going to even
tell you how it went,

00:46:54.400 --> 00:46:56.130
because it may be that I get something

00:46:56.130 --> 00:46:57.890
that I feel like is just for me

00:46:57.890 --> 00:47:00.820
and to share it would
make it, would ruin it.

00:47:00.820 --> 00:47:04.403
So it may be that I'll
wait and share it later.

00:47:05.690 --> 00:47:09.050
Cause I honestly, I don't,
I'm just trying to be open.

00:47:09.050 --> 00:47:11.060
I am going to try to
make contact with aliens.

00:47:11.060 --> 00:47:12.760
That is one of the things
that is going to happen.

00:47:12.760 --> 00:47:16.474
Well, okay.

00:47:16.474 --> 00:47:19.850
You're talking about
after that Netflix rec.

00:47:19.850 --> 00:47:21.220
No, I know we we've talked,

00:47:21.220 --> 00:47:22.690
there's been a number of
documentaries that we've watched.

00:47:22.690 --> 00:47:24.650
Well, okay. So again--

00:47:24.650 --> 00:47:27.410
That seems like a totally different path.

00:47:27.410 --> 00:47:30.800
Yeah, we'll talk about this more later,

00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:33.020
but, and here's the thing,

00:47:33.020 --> 00:47:36.000
I don't believe that any of this is real,

00:47:36.000 --> 00:47:38.880
but I'm just trying to be a person

00:47:38.880 --> 00:47:41.410
who doesn't just conclude things

00:47:41.410 --> 00:47:45.140
before being open to them.

00:47:45.140 --> 00:47:47.500
And the whole Dr Steven Greer thing,

00:47:47.500 --> 00:47:49.790
he's got a couple of
documentaries on Netflix.

00:47:49.790 --> 00:47:52.590
He's the guy that had some access,

00:47:52.590 --> 00:47:54.530
he worked at area 51 or whatever,

00:47:54.530 --> 00:47:57.260
and he swears that
there's extra terrestrials

00:47:57.260 --> 00:48:00.330
and they are, people are
in contact with them.

00:48:00.330 --> 00:48:04.460
And then he has this whole
app where the idea is

00:48:04.460 --> 00:48:07.820
that through meditation,
usually group meditation,

00:48:07.820 --> 00:48:11.520
you can make contact with these aliens.

00:48:11.520 --> 00:48:14.320
Now do I believe that this
is what's actually happening?

00:48:15.390 --> 00:48:18.390
I would be so surprised if
that's what's actually happening,

00:48:18.390 --> 00:48:21.260
but if it was what was actually happening,

00:48:21.260 --> 00:48:23.530
wouldn't it be cool.

00:48:23.530 --> 00:48:24.740
You know what I mean?

00:48:24.740 --> 00:48:27.277
And so I'm just, again, coming from,

00:48:27.277 --> 00:48:31.960
and a lot of this is continuing
to peel back the layers

00:48:31.960 --> 00:48:35.133
of spending my entire life,

00:48:37.150 --> 00:48:39.440
up until about 10 years ago or so,

00:48:39.440 --> 00:48:43.550
really entrenched in an
evangelical worldview.

00:48:43.550 --> 00:48:46.300
And one of the things that
comes along, for me personally,

00:48:46.300 --> 00:48:50.066
with the evangelical
worldview, is just the belief

00:48:50.066 --> 00:48:54.320
that you have arrived
at the ultimate truth.

00:48:54.320 --> 00:48:57.350
I specifically remember,
even as a college student,

00:48:57.350 --> 00:49:02.350
thinking, man it's so cool that
I believe the correct thing.

00:49:03.211 --> 00:49:08.160
It's so cool that I know
that Jesus is the only way

00:49:08.160 --> 00:49:10.320
to have a connection with
the creator of the universe,

00:49:10.320 --> 00:49:12.210
and that I have a relationship with him,

00:49:12.210 --> 00:49:14.460
and that I have arrived at this truth

00:49:14.460 --> 00:49:15.830
that is the ultimate truth.

00:49:15.830 --> 00:49:18.740
I remember thinking that
as a college student.

00:49:18.740 --> 00:49:21.320
And 20 years later, I'm at this
place where it's just like,

00:49:21.320 --> 00:49:24.550
the only thing I know is
that I don't know anything.

00:49:24.550 --> 00:49:26.570
And it's a completely
different place to be.

00:49:26.570 --> 00:49:28.910
But when you have this worldview

00:49:28.910 --> 00:49:33.670
that it's all about having
this systematic theology,

00:49:33.670 --> 00:49:35.720
all this stuff kind of wrapped up together

00:49:35.720 --> 00:49:38.010
and it's kind of impenetrable, right?

00:49:38.010 --> 00:49:40.290
And you're not really supposed to poke it.

00:49:40.290 --> 00:49:42.110
And if you do poke it,
you're supposed to do it

00:49:42.110 --> 00:49:43.680
for the sake of just building it up

00:49:43.680 --> 00:49:45.730
and make it even making it even stronger.

00:49:46.580 --> 00:49:49.640
To me, it's a good
exercise for me to be like,

00:49:49.640 --> 00:49:53.420
now I have absolutely no reason to believe

00:49:53.420 --> 00:49:55.950
that I'm going to have
contact with aliens,

00:49:55.950 --> 00:50:00.040
but what does it feel like to sit down,

00:50:00.040 --> 00:50:03.190
in the middle of the desert,
and I actually bought,

00:50:03.190 --> 00:50:06.250
because they suggested
that you buy this chair.

00:50:06.250 --> 00:50:09.440
That is one of those chairs,
the antigravity chair,

00:50:09.440 --> 00:50:10.632
basically that you can kinda lean back.

00:50:10.632 --> 00:50:13.790
You float? Okay, a recliner.

00:50:13.790 --> 00:50:16.450
It's basically a recliner
for the desert or the beach.

00:50:16.450 --> 00:50:18.090
An alien recliner.

00:50:18.090 --> 00:50:19.550
And stare at the sky.

00:50:19.550 --> 00:50:21.430
Does it, it points your butt hole

00:50:21.430 --> 00:50:22.790
in the right place for a probe?

00:50:22.790 --> 00:50:26.496
Right, yeah. It opens
you straight up to it.

00:50:26.496 --> 00:50:29.340
There's going to be a moment where I am--

00:50:29.340 --> 00:50:30.520
Just relax, let it in.

00:50:30.520 --> 00:50:33.393
In a place where I'm out there.

00:50:33.393 --> 00:50:36.350
It's just me and nature.

00:50:36.350 --> 00:50:40.010
And I'm going to be open to
extra terrestrial interaction.

00:50:40.010 --> 00:50:41.020
Now, Rhett--

00:50:41.020 --> 00:50:43.160
And if it happens, I will talk about it.

00:50:43.160 --> 00:50:45.010
We remember what happened

00:50:45.010 --> 00:50:47.230
when you got scared on
your solo trip and you ran

00:50:47.230 --> 00:50:50.920
into your tent and watched
Superbad on your laptop.

00:50:50.920 --> 00:50:55.110
I certainly expect that that
is going to be a struggle.

00:50:55.110 --> 00:50:56.950
I certainly expect--
You're gonna get scared.

00:50:56.950 --> 00:51:00.490
That being scared, and
the funny thing about that

00:51:00.490 --> 00:51:03.150
is that I actually could hear the highway

00:51:03.150 --> 00:51:06.050
and see cars a couple of miles away.

00:51:06.050 --> 00:51:07.510
I'm going to be in some places,

00:51:07.510 --> 00:51:10.780
if I can get to the places
that I want to go, where,

00:51:10.780 --> 00:51:12.530
like I have a satellite phone, FYI.

00:51:13.865 --> 00:51:16.240
'Cause I'm going to be by
myself and I'm going to be

00:51:16.240 --> 00:51:18.910
well outside of any sort of cell service.

00:51:18.910 --> 00:51:23.910
I've got a satellite phone
that sends, oh and by the way,

00:51:24.010 --> 00:51:26.500
you're listed as the
second emergency contact

00:51:26.500 --> 00:51:29.270
behind my wife, so,
which may not be great,

00:51:29.270 --> 00:51:31.920
'cause you're going to
be on your own trip.

00:51:31.920 --> 00:51:34.040
But I will have the ability to do an SOS.

00:51:34.040 --> 00:51:38.450
I have the ability to text
and basically text my location

00:51:38.450 --> 00:51:40.280
and I can get somebody to come rescue me,

00:51:40.280 --> 00:51:43.173
for a lot of money, if
things get real bad.

00:51:46.400 --> 00:51:47.233
Okay.

00:51:47.233 --> 00:51:50.400
But I plan, I am definitely
going to get scared.

00:51:50.400 --> 00:51:53.780
I definitely relate to
the expectation thing.

00:51:53.780 --> 00:51:54.613
I mean,

00:51:55.850 --> 00:52:00.743
in general, in my life,
I'm trying to deal with,

00:52:03.480 --> 00:52:06.220
how I place expectations on things,

00:52:06.220 --> 00:52:10.640
and how I seek to control
things, and perfect things.

00:52:10.640 --> 00:52:15.640
And one of the questions
that I'm learning to ask is

00:52:15.990 --> 00:52:18.280
what is my desired outcome?

00:52:18.280 --> 00:52:21.170
Because I've, and through that,

00:52:21.170 --> 00:52:23.700
I noticed that a lot
of the things that I do

00:52:23.700 --> 00:52:26.670
and actions that I take to assert control

00:52:26.670 --> 00:52:28.000
that make me feel good,

00:52:28.000 --> 00:52:32.240
actually don't move me
towards the desired outcome,

00:52:32.240 --> 00:52:34.540
if I were to state what that is.

00:52:34.540 --> 00:52:36.750
Now that's actually different than,

00:52:36.750 --> 00:52:39.393
I think you're describing
an exercise that is,

00:52:40.730 --> 00:52:43.430
let go of desire for an outcome.

00:52:43.430 --> 00:52:45.120
So I'm not going to say that.

00:52:45.120 --> 00:52:47.610
Whoa, you're moving the whole table.

00:52:47.610 --> 00:52:49.551
Well, you keep hitting the
table, and it's making noise,

00:52:49.551 --> 00:52:51.489
and I'm trying to--

00:52:51.489 --> 00:52:53.320
Well, what you're doing
is not making noise.

00:52:53.320 --> 00:52:54.220
I made it worse.

00:52:56.490 --> 00:52:57.900
That got it. That's good enough.

00:52:57.900 --> 00:53:00.130
That's basically where it was.

00:53:00.130 --> 00:53:04.760
Just embrace the wobbliness of the table.

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:07.840
This is what we found. Here we are.

00:53:07.840 --> 00:53:09.310
Right. That's good. This is good exercise.

00:53:09.310 --> 00:53:10.143
Be here now.

00:53:10.143 --> 00:53:11.250
And I usually don't care
about this kind of thing.

00:53:11.250 --> 00:53:12.947
Usually you would be the
one that cared about it.

00:53:12.947 --> 00:53:14.820
I know. I was making a point.

00:53:14.820 --> 00:53:15.910
Okay. Good.

00:53:15.910 --> 00:53:18.470
I don't remember it because
you shimmied the table.

00:53:18.470 --> 00:53:20.210
That was a test.
Aggressively.

00:53:20.210 --> 00:53:21.043
It was a test.

00:53:23.570 --> 00:53:26.310
I think those are, I mean,
they're two different,

00:53:26.310 --> 00:53:30.540
knowing what my desired outcome
is for me and stating that

00:53:30.540 --> 00:53:34.500
is just a, is an exercise to help me know

00:53:34.500 --> 00:53:36.880
if I'm fixating on things
for the wrong reason,

00:53:36.880 --> 00:53:38.330
just for the sake of control.

00:53:39.170 --> 00:53:41.340
I think it's just a different exercise

00:53:41.340 --> 00:53:43.210
what you're doing.

00:53:43.210 --> 00:53:46.830
But I do think there's
an element of that for me

00:53:46.830 --> 00:53:49.410
in this trip as well, that I'm trying to.

00:53:49.410 --> 00:53:51.850
Okay, my desired outcome

00:53:51.850 --> 00:53:55.470
is to have

00:53:55.470 --> 00:53:58.040
a quality experience with Christy,

00:53:58.040 --> 00:53:59.360
for us to have a good time together.

00:53:59.360 --> 00:54:01.930
For us to come back and have
a good time. Just period.

00:54:01.930 --> 00:54:04.680
You know, we had to cancel
our 20 year anniversary trip.

00:54:04.680 --> 00:54:07.040
We were going to go to Big
Sur and stay in this cabin.

00:54:07.040 --> 00:54:08.450
It was going to be really cool.

00:54:08.450 --> 00:54:10.630
We had to cancel all of
that because of COVID.

00:54:10.630 --> 00:54:14.070
And instead of trying to
rebook something like that,

00:54:14.070 --> 00:54:17.590
I'm going with this van
dream, test type thing.

00:54:17.590 --> 00:54:21.390
But yeah, I could very easily
put so much pressure on her

00:54:23.090 --> 00:54:26.080
to have a good time,
and to like this thing,

00:54:26.080 --> 00:54:30.310
and to embrace my dream
and fantasy for us,

00:54:30.310 --> 00:54:33.430
like living the van life.

00:54:33.430 --> 00:54:37.090
Or/and put so much pressure on myself

00:54:37.090 --> 00:54:40.030
to create an experience
that would win her over.

00:54:40.030 --> 00:54:44.380
Versus this may be the only
experience we have in a van.

00:54:44.380 --> 00:54:45.860
It may suck. It may be great.

00:54:45.860 --> 00:54:47.950
But it's gonna, we're gonna be together.

00:54:47.950 --> 00:54:50.610
And it's, I just want to
set it up for quality.

00:54:50.610 --> 00:54:53.550
And it's not about going
to a certain destination

00:54:53.550 --> 00:54:54.660
and then saying, okay,

00:54:54.660 --> 00:54:57.220
well if we go here, these are the pictures

00:54:57.220 --> 00:54:58.570
all of these people take on Instagram.

00:54:58.570 --> 00:55:00.410
These are the things we gotta see, okay.

00:55:00.410 --> 00:55:02.180
That means we've got to do this trail.

00:55:02.180 --> 00:55:03.530
We got to hike this trail.

00:55:03.530 --> 00:55:05.020
Well that means we've got
to get on this shuttle.

00:55:05.020 --> 00:55:05.870
That means we've got a park here.

00:55:05.870 --> 00:55:06.900
That means we've got to, you know,

00:55:06.900 --> 00:55:09.150
all of these things that are about,

00:55:09.150 --> 00:55:14.050
well my desired outcome is not
to have Instagramable moments

00:55:14.050 --> 00:55:18.010
or be able to say that I did,

00:55:18.010 --> 00:55:20.360
when I say I went to Bryce
Canyon and someone says,

00:55:20.360 --> 00:55:21.790
Oh, did you do the so-and-so?

00:55:21.790 --> 00:55:25.040
It doesn't matter if my
answer is yes or no to them.

00:55:25.040 --> 00:55:29.090
It's interesting how I can
fall into that trap so easily.

00:55:29.090 --> 00:55:30.590
It's like, unless I meet someone

00:55:30.590 --> 00:55:32.850
who knows more than me about
something that I'm doing,

00:55:32.850 --> 00:55:34.640
if I don't meet their expectations,

00:55:34.640 --> 00:55:37.030
then I failed because I haven't done,

00:55:40.207 --> 00:55:42.020
I haven't had a perfect trip.

00:55:42.020 --> 00:55:42.853
And there's a fear--

00:55:42.853 --> 00:55:43.686
Oh well, you didn't see the so-and-so.

00:55:43.686 --> 00:55:45.570
And then there's the
fear of missing out too.

00:55:45.570 --> 00:55:47.340
I mean, I remember the first time

00:55:48.970 --> 00:55:50.820
we went to Disney world

00:55:50.820 --> 00:55:53.570
with my wife's family, right?

00:55:53.570 --> 00:55:55.290
So this is a big trip.

00:55:55.290 --> 00:55:58.490
Her parents, I guess, at that point,

00:55:58.490 --> 00:56:00.240
we may or may not have had any kids.

00:56:00.240 --> 00:56:01.163
I can't remember.

00:56:02.666 --> 00:56:06.840
But my brother and sister
in-law had at least a kid.

00:56:06.840 --> 00:56:10.063
And then we had Gaga and Papa with us.

00:56:11.110 --> 00:56:12.280
May they both rest in peace,

00:56:12.280 --> 00:56:13.590
but they were both alive at the time.

00:56:13.590 --> 00:56:15.230
Okay, that makes it easier.

00:56:15.230 --> 00:56:18.050
And the idea,

00:56:18.050 --> 00:56:19.110
so what I did,

00:56:19.110 --> 00:56:21.410
when I found out we were
going to Disney world.

00:56:21.410 --> 00:56:23.290
Itinerary, man.

00:56:23.290 --> 00:56:25.280
And here's, the funny
thing is, I talk about it,

00:56:25.280 --> 00:56:28.700
like I, when somebody,

00:56:28.700 --> 00:56:33.700
when your best friend is as
efficiency driven as you are,

00:56:34.270 --> 00:56:38.010
you begin to think that you're not.

00:56:38.010 --> 00:56:41.100
You begin to think that you're
this happy go-lucky guy,

00:56:41.100 --> 00:56:43.890
until you interact with normal people

00:56:43.890 --> 00:56:46.620
or people who are on the
opposite end of the spectrum.

00:56:46.620 --> 00:56:49.780
And then you realize
that, I realized that I am

00:56:49.780 --> 00:56:52.800
so much more concerned about
planning and efficiency

00:56:52.800 --> 00:56:54.493
then my wife's family.

00:56:55.440 --> 00:56:57.820
And also, probably, than
the average person, right.

00:56:57.820 --> 00:56:59.810
Or I'm probably somewhere in
the middle of the spectrum.

00:56:59.810 --> 00:57:03.363
But for this trip I bought the book.

00:57:04.575 --> 00:57:07.720
And I was like, okay,
we've got five days here.

00:57:07.720 --> 00:57:09.350
These are the parks we need to visit.

00:57:09.350 --> 00:57:12.660
This is the, we need to
literally go around the park

00:57:12.660 --> 00:57:15.990
in this direction, we need to
get fast passes for this ride.

00:57:15.990 --> 00:57:17.450
We need to skip this ride.

00:57:17.450 --> 00:57:18.283
And I was like, if you,

00:57:18.283 --> 00:57:20.080
cause we want to hit all the hotspots.

00:57:20.080 --> 00:57:22.050
So I remember--
But that wasn't--

00:57:22.050 --> 00:57:24.720
Breaking that plan out for them.

00:57:24.720 --> 00:57:29.720
And it was almost like,
okay, Mr Ruin Everyone's Fun.

00:57:30.910 --> 00:57:33.860
You know what I'm saying?
That was their take on it.

00:57:33.860 --> 00:57:36.210
Their philosophy was let's just go in.

00:57:36.210 --> 00:57:39.480
Let's, you don't, why do
we have to get up so early,

00:57:39.480 --> 00:57:41.320
and have breakfast, and
get there before people,

00:57:41.320 --> 00:57:42.440
and make sure you do this.

00:57:42.440 --> 00:57:43.850
Can't we just go in there?

00:57:43.850 --> 00:57:45.460
Now there is a balance.

00:57:45.460 --> 00:57:46.580
Let me just say there is a balance

00:57:46.580 --> 00:57:49.070
because if you take the complete opposite,

00:57:49.070 --> 00:57:51.520
no planning, no foresight,

00:57:51.520 --> 00:57:53.530
you might go and be like,
we didn't do anything fun.

00:57:53.530 --> 00:57:55.220
All I did was wait in two lines all day

00:57:55.220 --> 00:57:56.870
'cause I didn't think about this.

00:57:57.875 --> 00:58:00.580
But when you get in my,
that's what I'm trying to,

00:58:00.580 --> 00:58:02.190
I'm trying to strike the balance.

00:58:02.190 --> 00:58:06.050
The balance between being
prepared and having a plan,

00:58:06.050 --> 00:58:10.180
but having no expectation
that that plan will be met

00:58:10.180 --> 00:58:13.410
and not thinking that success

00:58:13.410 --> 00:58:15.710
is the plan being accomplished.

00:58:15.710 --> 00:58:16.650
Right.

00:58:16.650 --> 00:58:17.850
These certain expectations.

00:58:17.850 --> 00:58:20.780
So being prepared, but
having no expectations,

00:58:20.780 --> 00:58:22.740
it's like those, those
are two very different--

00:58:22.740 --> 00:58:23.740
Maybe we're saying--

00:58:23.740 --> 00:58:24.945
I think we're saying the same thing.

00:58:24.945 --> 00:58:25.778
Maybe we're saying the same thing.

00:58:25.778 --> 00:58:28.580
'Cause I'm like, if I
say my desired outcome

00:58:28.580 --> 00:58:33.580
is to enjoy Christy's company

00:58:33.850 --> 00:58:35.687
and for her to enjoy mine.

00:58:35.687 --> 00:58:39.580
And that means I have to
stay in a certain mind frame.

00:58:39.580 --> 00:58:42.210
That's enjoyable, you know.

00:58:42.210 --> 00:58:45.120
I can't fall from my
own traps, which make me

00:58:45.120 --> 00:58:48.370
someone who's not fun to be
around because I get in my head

00:58:48.370 --> 00:58:51.281
about, oh, this isn't
working out, I'm a failure.

00:58:51.281 --> 00:58:53.140
But also you stop having fun.

00:58:53.140 --> 00:58:55.560
Oh yeah, yeah, definitely.

00:58:55.560 --> 00:58:58.100
So it's, if that's my
desired outcome, then it's,

00:58:58.100 --> 00:59:00.010
oh, it's not about going
on the right trail,

00:59:00.010 --> 00:59:01.270
or getting to this certain place,

00:59:01.270 --> 00:59:05.180
or camping at the place
with the most perfect view.

00:59:05.180 --> 00:59:08.453
And then if it happens,
you're like, wow, bonus.

00:59:10.200 --> 00:59:12.650
Is that the same, is that
similar to what you're saying,

00:59:12.650 --> 00:59:14.670
in terms of letting go of expectations?

00:59:14.670 --> 00:59:15.880
Yeah. It's the same thing.

00:59:15.880 --> 00:59:19.440
I mean, for you, again, I
think this is that whole

00:59:21.633 --> 00:59:23.420
enneagram one, enneagram three,

00:59:23.420 --> 00:59:25.090
presenting in a very similar way

00:59:25.090 --> 00:59:27.540
in the way that they approach things.

00:59:27.540 --> 00:59:30.810
For you it might be about controlling it

00:59:30.810 --> 00:59:33.480
and doing it perfectly.

00:59:33.480 --> 00:59:37.340
And for me it might be a
slightly different twist on that

00:59:37.340 --> 00:59:40.586
of just like accomplishing
a certain number of things.

00:59:40.586 --> 00:59:43.680
In it's effect, it's
kind of the same thing.

00:59:43.680 --> 00:59:46.240
It's like, I'm going into this trip.

00:59:46.240 --> 00:59:47.747
I'm thinking that, now I don't have,

00:59:47.747 --> 00:59:51.200
and because I am not
trying to go to anything,

00:59:51.200 --> 00:59:53.080
other than there's a couple of hot springs

00:59:53.080 --> 00:59:54.920
that I definitely want to see.

00:59:54.920 --> 00:59:57.420
So if I didn't see those, if
I didn't make it to those,

00:59:57.420 --> 01:00:00.398
or something about that
aspect of it was screwed up.

01:00:00.398 --> 01:00:03.170
That's gonna present
itself as a disappointment.

01:00:03.170 --> 01:00:04.790
But it's not really a sightseeing trip.

01:00:04.790 --> 01:00:05.930
It may be the case

01:00:05.930 --> 01:00:10.690
that I drive into the
wilderness on day one.

01:00:10.690 --> 01:00:13.670
And then I'm just like, I'm
going to stay here for six days.

01:00:13.670 --> 01:00:16.530
I'm gonna keep my truck right here.

01:00:16.530 --> 01:00:17.980
And I'm just gonna stay here.

01:00:19.488 --> 01:00:20.900
And be okay with that.

01:00:20.900 --> 01:00:22.210
'Cause being alone and driving,

01:00:22.210 --> 01:00:26.163
and being alone in one
place, is a different thing.

01:00:27.020 --> 01:00:30.070
I do expect at least one of the places

01:00:30.070 --> 01:00:31.880
to be a place that I would be like, okay.

01:00:31.880 --> 01:00:35.670
'Cause it's not like every
morning I'm going to wake up.

01:00:35.670 --> 01:00:37.240
I'm going to eat some
breakfast really quickly.

01:00:37.240 --> 01:00:38.370
And then I'm going to fold my tent up

01:00:38.370 --> 01:00:40.526
and just get back on the road.

01:00:40.526 --> 01:00:42.850
I fully expect that I'll be like,

01:00:42.850 --> 01:00:44.350
well today I'm just going to stay here.

01:00:44.350 --> 01:00:45.183
I'm going to sleep in
the same exact place.

01:00:45.183 --> 01:00:46.860
At what point do you think
you're going to start

01:00:46.860 --> 01:00:49.800
speaking audibly to yourself?
Early on.

01:00:49.800 --> 01:00:52.130
Early on, huh?
Yeah.

01:00:52.130 --> 01:00:55.160
Yeah. I wonder, I wonder if I would speak.

01:00:55.160 --> 01:00:56.850
I'm not even going to, there's
not going to be a time.

01:00:56.850 --> 01:00:58.020
I would do that anyway.

01:00:58.020 --> 01:00:59.210
Yeah. I think it would,

01:00:59.210 --> 01:01:01.597
it would take me a good number of days

01:01:01.597 --> 01:01:03.963
before I start speaking
out loud to myself.

01:01:04.940 --> 01:01:06.010
But then once I did it,

01:01:06.010 --> 01:01:10.600
maybe that would open up a whole
stream of self realization.

01:01:10.600 --> 01:01:12.840
Well, the thing is, I'm
trying to figure out

01:01:12.840 --> 01:01:14.860
what is the best way to document it.

01:01:14.860 --> 01:01:19.860
Again, I often will journal something

01:01:20.540 --> 01:01:22.470
and I'll journal it in a way as if

01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:24.360
it will be read in the future.

01:01:24.360 --> 01:01:26.940
Because I cause, well, case in point,

01:01:26.940 --> 01:01:30.490
when we did the the
deconstruction, the lost years,

01:01:30.490 --> 01:01:32.317
I read from my journal.

01:01:32.317 --> 01:01:35.310
And I am

01:01:36.280 --> 01:01:40.490
narcissistic enough to have this idea

01:01:40.490 --> 01:01:43.190
that someone will be interested
in reading my journal.

01:01:44.290 --> 01:01:47.278
And the idea that for
this thing, it's like,

01:01:47.278 --> 01:01:48.650
okay, well what am I going to do?

01:01:48.650 --> 01:01:49.590
Am I gonna--

01:01:49.590 --> 01:01:51.520
You haven't decided
what you're going to do?

01:01:51.520 --> 01:01:52.940
Well I've got multiple options.

01:01:52.940 --> 01:01:55.360
I've got, I mean, I'm going
to have my computer with me.

01:01:55.360 --> 01:01:57.910
I'm going to take my
computer for typing things.

01:01:57.910 --> 01:01:59.940
But I was also, there was
a part of me that was like,

01:01:59.940 --> 01:02:04.940
what if I just take a pen and a notebook?

01:02:06.030 --> 01:02:08.690
I don't write well, and I get

01:02:08.690 --> 01:02:10.910
some carpal tunnel situations
when I try to write,

01:02:10.910 --> 01:02:13.490
and I have writer's fatigue with my hand,

01:02:13.490 --> 01:02:15.100
and much better at typing.

01:02:15.100 --> 01:02:16.920
But then I was like, should
I just do voice memos?

01:02:16.920 --> 01:02:17.760
Should I do a video?

01:02:17.760 --> 01:02:19.430
Don't do a video because
then you'll tempted

01:02:19.430 --> 01:02:21.750
to film it in a way that can
be turned into something.

01:02:21.750 --> 01:02:24.050
And then I'm like,
well, I've got my drone.

01:02:24.050 --> 01:02:25.240
And it would be really interesting

01:02:25.240 --> 01:02:29.740
to get a drone shot of everywhere
I stayed, for my own sake.

01:02:29.740 --> 01:02:31.210
But you know, when I'm doing that,

01:02:31.210 --> 01:02:33.030
I'm going to be thinking
about, well one day,

01:02:33.030 --> 01:02:35.960
not anytime soon, but years
from now, I'll be like,

01:02:35.960 --> 01:02:38.570
I went on this trip and
here's all the drone footage.

01:02:38.570 --> 01:02:39.720
Maybe next week.

01:02:39.720 --> 01:02:43.760
And so that's what I'm
struggling with right now.

01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:45.870
'Cause I also have, I've got
my, I've got lots of tech.

01:02:45.870 --> 01:02:47.500
So I've got my 360 camera.

01:02:47.500 --> 01:02:48.333
So I'm like, okay,

01:02:48.333 --> 01:02:50.640
I could do a 360 shot of every campsite.

01:02:50.640 --> 01:02:53.190
And that again, I've done that
in the past because it's cool

01:02:53.190 --> 01:02:56.080
to be able to put VR
on and be there again.

01:02:56.080 --> 01:02:58.351
I think you should do
the 360 camera thing.

01:02:58.351 --> 01:03:00.350
That's nice to be able to.

01:03:00.350 --> 01:03:03.420
I mean, if you're spending time at a spot

01:03:03.420 --> 01:03:06.170
and you're like, you should, I mean,

01:03:06.170 --> 01:03:07.760
obviously you're going to journal.

01:03:07.760 --> 01:03:09.040
I think that's a good idea.

01:03:09.040 --> 01:03:13.320
'Cause then you can, at
certain moments of insight

01:03:14.310 --> 01:03:16.310
in my past, it's like, it's nice,

01:03:16.310 --> 01:03:18.700
like if I was listening to certain music,

01:03:18.700 --> 01:03:20.450
it's nice to put that music back on.

01:03:20.450 --> 01:03:23.263
And it's a way to go back there.

01:03:24.710 --> 01:03:26.150
So the VR thing is another way,

01:03:26.150 --> 01:03:28.530
like literally you could
go back to that spot

01:03:29.800 --> 01:03:31.080
if you're listening to music

01:03:31.080 --> 01:03:34.420
and you're on VR in the spot again,

01:03:34.420 --> 01:03:38.010
it could really, magically,
bring you back to a spot

01:03:38.010 --> 01:03:39.950
where it could be special for you.

01:03:39.950 --> 01:03:41.323
I think so, I think so.

01:03:41.323 --> 01:03:45.200
Like a happy place, or
maybe it's a sad place.

01:03:45.200 --> 01:03:47.220
It's a poignant place.

01:03:47.220 --> 01:03:49.293
So I think that's a cool idea.

01:03:50.930 --> 01:03:53.660
Yeah. The video thing is,
that would be difficult.

01:03:53.660 --> 01:03:55.430
But like pictures. I mean, again,

01:03:55.430 --> 01:03:57.643
we've talked about this
on a whole episode.

01:03:57.643 --> 01:04:01.020
You got to take some
pictures, just do it for you.

01:04:01.020 --> 01:04:02.960
Yeah. And again, that's the thing.

01:04:02.960 --> 01:04:07.250
It's like, how can I be in
the, and this is it's really,

01:04:07.250 --> 01:04:12.250
this is just a microcosm of
what I want my life to be.

01:04:12.460 --> 01:04:14.510
And this is a whole 'nother can of worms.

01:04:15.773 --> 01:04:19.563
But how can I be in the world in a way

01:04:21.330 --> 01:04:26.330
that isn't about look at me
and look at what I can do?

01:04:27.170 --> 01:04:29.210
And that's a very
difficult thing for someone

01:04:29.210 --> 01:04:32.580
who makes a living saying,
look at what I can do.

01:04:32.580 --> 01:04:35.713
Or saying, if you don't look
at what I can do and enjoy it,

01:04:35.713 --> 01:04:38.200
then I don't make a living,
I don't have a company.

01:04:38.200 --> 01:04:39.400
The hair thing

01:04:41.530 --> 01:04:45.630
is an easy place to
point for that quandary.

01:04:45.630 --> 01:04:50.470
Because as we discussed, you
have your reasons for doing it,

01:04:50.470 --> 01:04:54.460
yet you knew, at the time,

01:04:54.460 --> 01:04:56.550
and you've definitely seen it playing out,

01:04:56.550 --> 01:05:00.313
that people have to comment
on how big your hair is.

01:05:01.490 --> 01:05:02.360
How big your beard is.

01:05:02.360 --> 01:05:03.240
That type, so you knew

01:05:03.240 --> 01:05:06.830
that it was going to present
some sort of tension.

01:05:09.530 --> 01:05:11.300
And I think that there's--

01:05:11.300 --> 01:05:12.360
So what's the update?

01:05:12.360 --> 01:05:14.310
I'm curious on the update there.

01:05:14.310 --> 01:05:15.680
Update on my hair?

01:05:15.680 --> 01:05:20.640
Well, I mean, it was, you did
it as a form of embodiment.

01:05:20.640 --> 01:05:22.070
It's related to all of these things.

01:05:22.070 --> 01:05:24.760
It's like it's a physical
representation of something

01:05:24.760 --> 01:05:28.090
that is going on within
you and your mindset.

01:05:28.090 --> 01:05:30.690
But you knew that you would,

01:05:30.690 --> 01:05:33.040
you have to deal with
people's reaction to it,

01:05:33.040 --> 01:05:34.710
response to, it discussion of it.

01:05:34.710 --> 01:05:37.610
Well, I think I'm kind
of past the point of,

01:05:37.610 --> 01:05:40.103
I'm not past it, in other words.

01:05:41.510 --> 01:05:44.540
Yeah, I'm fully aware of that dynamic

01:05:44.540 --> 01:05:47.020
and that struggle of it being like,

01:05:47.020 --> 01:05:49.320
oh, well people were saying
they really liked my hair.

01:05:49.320 --> 01:05:51.450
How do I not gravitate towards

01:05:51.450 --> 01:05:53.450
that type of commentary about it?

01:05:53.450 --> 01:05:56.550
And actually get something from it.

01:05:56.550 --> 01:05:58.380
It's rewarding to have people talk

01:05:58.380 --> 01:06:00.980
about how they like your hair, right?

01:06:00.980 --> 01:06:04.720
For me, it's more about

01:06:04.720 --> 01:06:07.310
this idea that when I

01:06:09.540 --> 01:06:13.120
look at pictures before
I grew my hair out,

01:06:13.120 --> 01:06:15.083
it feels less like me.

01:06:15.970 --> 01:06:16.850
Now, I'm not saying

01:06:16.850 --> 01:06:19.720
I'm not going to go back
to short hair or whatever.

01:06:19.720 --> 01:06:21.930
I'm not saying I'm gonna
have long hair forever.

01:06:21.930 --> 01:06:25.530
But I do think that
part of the exercise was

01:06:25.530 --> 01:06:28.373
you have this, I think that life is about,

01:06:29.740 --> 01:06:32.173
to use a meme, becoming your final form.

01:06:36.360 --> 01:06:38.700
And I think this is what every
religion teaches ultimately.

01:06:38.700 --> 01:06:40.480
Is like, you are trying

01:06:40.480 --> 01:06:44.370
to continue to move closer to something.

01:06:44.370 --> 01:06:47.150
If it's an Eastern philosophy,
it might be enlightenment.

01:06:47.150 --> 01:06:47.983
Christianity is like,

01:06:47.983 --> 01:06:50.410
you're trying to become
more and more Christlike.

01:06:50.410 --> 01:06:52.960
We're kind of talking about
very similar things of,

01:06:53.950 --> 01:06:58.457
trying, having some sort
of trajectory in your life.

01:07:00.160 --> 01:07:05.160
And for me, this idea of getting
more in touch with myself,

01:07:05.550 --> 01:07:08.500
not just being in my head all
the time, following my heart,

01:07:09.420 --> 01:07:14.420
I have begun to feel a
cohesiveness with that,

01:07:14.730 --> 01:07:19.523
when it comes to having
a big beard and big hair.

01:07:20.760 --> 01:07:23.900
So that aspect of it is like,
not mission accomplished,

01:07:23.900 --> 01:07:28.370
but sensing that, yes, that
there is something to that.

01:07:28.370 --> 01:07:32.210
I feel that I look more,

01:07:32.210 --> 01:07:37.163
I think I look more like I
feel about the world now.

01:07:39.560 --> 01:07:40.470
So that's the update

01:07:40.470 --> 01:07:43.063
is that that has happened to some degree.

01:07:44.055 --> 01:07:46.663
I don't know where it's
gonna go from here.

01:07:50.330 --> 01:07:51.423
So next week,

01:07:53.260 --> 01:07:54.720
next time we record

01:07:54.720 --> 01:07:55.869
it will be after the trip.

01:07:55.869 --> 01:07:58.440
'Cause we're about to go on these trips.

01:07:58.440 --> 01:08:01.754
Who knows, if we'll even
decide to talk about it at all.

01:08:01.754 --> 01:08:03.670
It seems like I've got a lot more leeway

01:08:03.670 --> 01:08:07.060
to talk about it than
you do, but maybe not.

01:08:07.060 --> 01:08:09.453
Well that was the last thing
I was going to say was--

01:08:09.453 --> 01:08:11.340
It's not a desired outcome of mine.

01:08:11.340 --> 01:08:14.640
I think I have to get to a place where

01:08:15.960 --> 01:08:19.300
I can't expect the environment

01:08:19.300 --> 01:08:24.080
and the way that the world works to change

01:08:24.080 --> 01:08:25.583
in order for me to be okay.

01:08:28.110 --> 01:08:30.790
I can't expect people to stop talking

01:08:30.790 --> 01:08:32.833
about a change that I make physically.

01:08:33.684 --> 01:08:35.400
That's going to continue to happen

01:08:35.400 --> 01:08:40.400
whether I'm on camera, on
people's computers, or not.

01:08:43.560 --> 01:08:46.330
But I could, but I do believe
I could get to a place

01:08:46.330 --> 01:08:48.180
where it really doesn't matter.

01:08:48.180 --> 01:08:51.250
And it's not about accolades

01:08:51.250 --> 01:08:54.910
or getting some sort of
feedback outside of myself.

01:08:54.910 --> 01:08:59.910
It's this idea that what I need
is not some external thing.

01:09:00.183 --> 01:09:01.810
It's not some validation.

01:09:01.810 --> 01:09:04.540
It's not my environment
being what it should be.

01:09:04.540 --> 01:09:09.070
I shouldn't have to curate a solo trip

01:09:09.070 --> 01:09:10.410
in order to get to the place

01:09:10.410 --> 01:09:12.760
that I want to get to
emotionally, spiritually.

01:09:13.609 --> 01:09:16.290
Now those may be helpful to do that.

01:09:16.290 --> 01:09:19.250
But ultimately, wouldn't we
all like to get to a place

01:09:19.250 --> 01:09:21.470
where, regardless of the circumstances,

01:09:21.470 --> 01:09:24.723
you had this equanimity
that you can access, right?

01:09:25.750 --> 01:09:29.410
And so I think that

01:09:32.180 --> 01:09:33.160
that's the challenge for me,

01:09:33.160 --> 01:09:36.110
is go and don't overthink it.

01:09:36.110 --> 01:09:38.760
You want to drone, you want
to break the drone out?

01:09:38.760 --> 01:09:41.025
Just break the drone
out, do it for yourself.

01:09:41.025 --> 01:09:45.080
If you don't do anything

01:09:45.080 --> 01:09:48.593
so that you can talk about it or share it,

01:09:50.300 --> 01:09:51.230
and then you come back

01:09:51.230 --> 01:09:53.640
and you want to talk about it or share it.

01:09:53.640 --> 01:09:55.340
Secondarily, go for it.
Right.

01:09:55.340 --> 01:09:57.830
Finding that, getting to a place

01:09:57.830 --> 01:10:00.457
where you can just be motivated
by, I just wanna do this.

01:10:00.457 --> 01:10:03.150
'Cause the only person who's
going to miss out is you.

01:10:03.150 --> 01:10:04.950
Right.
Or me.

01:10:04.950 --> 01:10:06.870
If that's our mentality.

01:10:06.870 --> 01:10:07.703
I mean,

01:10:10.040 --> 01:10:11.740
Christy may miss out on some of me

01:10:11.740 --> 01:10:13.340
and I may miss out on some of myself

01:10:13.340 --> 01:10:16.040
and you might miss out
on some of yourself,

01:10:16.040 --> 01:10:21.040
if you're doing things for
the effect or the story.

01:10:21.510 --> 01:10:23.160
So maybe you can tell me about it

01:10:25.280 --> 01:10:27.570
'cause I'm going to want to know.

01:10:27.570 --> 01:10:28.667
But don't think about me

01:10:28.667 --> 01:10:31.130
and don't think about
these people listening

01:10:31.130 --> 01:10:31.980
while you're out there.

01:10:31.980 --> 01:10:33.663
I don't think about you at all.

01:10:35.130 --> 01:10:37.800
And let's not get close to any fires.

01:10:37.800 --> 01:10:39.188
I'm committed to that.

01:10:39.188 --> 01:10:40.810
That's one thing we didn't talk about.

01:10:40.810 --> 01:10:42.790
We're not getting close to any fires.

01:10:42.790 --> 01:10:46.260
It's not necessarily just
staying away from the fires

01:10:46.260 --> 01:10:48.000
that are already happening.

